IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 203A (Part 6, Division 1): a summary financial statement sent to the members instead of the full documents.
-- The cases in which a company may do this, the form and information of the summary, and the manner of finding out whether a member wishes to receive it are
-- left to regulations (subsections (1), (5) and (9)): each is an input named for the fact, never a number or a list from memory.
-- Subsection (8) is shown deleted (Act 36 of 2014); subsection (9), the Minister's power to make regulations, is machinery (NOTES.md, inert reason 2).
-- "Default penalty" is s 408's: the penalty record says that one applies; its amount is not here.

DECLARE `s 203A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 203A(4) send copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1) to the member who wishes to receive them`
    `s 203A(6A) ensure that the summary financial statements comply with the requirements referred to in subsections (5) and (6)`

DECLARE `s 203A(7) penalty` HAS
    `s 203A(7) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203A(7) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 203A(7) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 203A(7) a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Section 203A(1): sending a summary instead`

-- src:18924 | 203A.—(1) Despite section 203 and anything in its constitution, a
-- src:18925 | company may, in such cases as may be specified by regulations and
-- src:18926 | provided all the conditions so specified are complied with, send a
-- src:18927 | summary financial statement instead of copies of the documents
-- src:18928 | referred to in section 203(1) to members of the company.
@ref s 203A(1) (src:18924-18928)
GIVEN `the case is one specified by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the conditions specified by regulations are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(1) the company may send a summary financial statement instead of copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the case is one specified by regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the cases are those "as may be specified by regulations", which are not among the sources
    ELSE IF `all the conditions specified by regulations are complied with`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in such cases as may be specified by regulations and provided all the conditions so specified are complied with" (a condition the text introduces with "provided": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2, keeps JUST FALSE where the text closes the gate itself)

§ `Section 203A(2): a member asks for the summary`

-- src:18932 | (2) Where a company sends to its members a summary financial
-- src:18933 | statement under subsection (1), any member of the company, and any
-- src:18934 | holder of a debenture, entitled to be furnished by the company with a
-- src:18935 | copy of the documents referred to in section 203(3) may instead
-- src:18936 | request for a summary financial statement.
@ref s 203A(2) (src:18932-18936)
GIVEN `the company sends to its members a summary financial statement under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company, or a holder of a debenture, entitled to be furnished with a copy of the documents referred to in section 203(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(2) the person may instead request a summary financial statement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a member of the company, or a holder of a debenture, entitled to be furnished with a copy of the documents referred to in section 203(3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the choice is given to "any member of the company, and any holder of a debenture, entitled to be furnished ... with a copy of the documents referred to in section 203(3)", and the subsection is silent on anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the company sends to its members a summary financial statement under subsection (1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company sends to its members a summary financial statement under subsection (1), any member of the company ... may instead request for a summary financial statement" (a "may" gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3, says do not change it and list it for the maintainer; fork F-203A-2, NOTES.md)

§ `Section 203A(3) and (4): the member who does or does not want it`

-- src:18940 | (3) A summary financial statement need not be sent to any member
-- src:18941 | of the company who does not wish to receive the statement.
@ref s 203A(3) (src:18940-18941)
GIVEN `the member does not wish to receive the summary financial statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(3) the company need not send the summary financial statement to the member` MEANS
    IF `the member does not wish to receive the summary financial statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A summary financial statement need not be sent to any member of the company who does not wish to receive the statement" (a "need not" limited to the member who does not wish; marginal reading (a), NOTES.md: the other reading is NOTHING, since the relief is grant-like and subsection (4) is what binds a member who wishes to receive copies)

-- src:18943 | (4) Copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1) must be
-- src:18944 | sent to any member of the company who wishes to receive them.
@ref s 203A(4) (src:18943-18944)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member wishes to receive copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(4) the company must send copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1) to the member` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company` AND `the member wishes to receive copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed to "any member of the company who wishes to receive them", and the subsection is silent on a member who does not wish, and on anyone who is not a member (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection (the consequence is the offence in subsection (7)): no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 203A(4) (src:18943-18944)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203A act`
`s 203A(4) the company must send copies of the documents to the member who wishes to receive them` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 203A(4) send copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1) to the member who wishes to receive them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not send copies of the documents referred to in section 203(1) to the member who wishes to receive them"

§ `Section 203A(5) and (6): what a summary financial statement must be`

-- src:18946 | (5) The summary financial statement must be derived from the
-- src:18947 | company’s annual financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18948 | statements, and directors’ statement and must be in such form and
-- src:18949 | contain such information as may be specified by regulations.
@ref s 203A(5) (src:18946-18949)
GIVEN `the summary financial statement is derived from the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary financial statement is in the form, and contains the information, that regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(5) the summary financial statement is derived and in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the summary financial statement is derived from the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement`
       AND `the summary financial statement is in the form, and contains the information, that regulations specify`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The summary financial statement must be derived from the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement and must be in such form and contain such information as may be specified by regulations" (a duty not met: the provision's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)

-- src:18953 | (6) Every summary financial statement must —
-- src:18955 | (a) state that it is only a summary of information in the
-- src:18956 | company’s annual financial statements or consolidated
-- src:18957 | financial statements, and directors’ statement; and
-- src:18962 | (b) contain a statement by the company’s auditors (if any) of
-- src:18963 | their opinion as to whether the summary financial
-- src:18964 | statement is consistent with the financial statements or
-- src:18965 | consolidated financial statements, and the directors’
-- src:18966 | statement and complies with the requirements of this
-- src:18967 | section and any regulations made under subsection (9).
@ref s 203A(6) (src:18953-18967)
GIVEN `the summary financial statement states that it is only a summary of information in the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary financial statement contains a statement by the company's auditors of their opinion on its consistency and compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(6) the summary financial statement contains the statements the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the summary financial statement states that it is only a summary of information in the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement`
       AND (IF `the company has auditors` THEN `the summary financial statement contains a statement by the company's auditors of their opinion on its consistency and compliance` ELSE TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every summary financial statement must — (a) state that it is only a summary ...; and (b) contain a statement by the company's auditors (if any) of their opinion" (a duty not met: the provision's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; "(if any)" means a company with no auditors owes no auditors' statement)

-- src:18971 | (6A) The directors of the company must ensure that the summary
-- src:18972 | financial statements comply with the requirements referred to in
-- src:18973 | subsections (5) and (6).
@ref s 203A(6A) (src:18971-18973)
GIVEN `the summary financial statement is derived from the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary financial statement is in the form, and contains the information, that regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary financial statement states that it is only a summary of information in the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary financial statement contains a statement by the company's auditors of their opinion on its consistency and compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(6A) the directors have ensured that the summary financial statements comply with subsections (5) and (6)` MEANS
    IF    `s 203A(5) the summary financial statement is derived and in the form the subsection requires` `the summary financial statement is derived from the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` `the summary financial statement is in the form, and contains the information, that regulations specify` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 203A(6) the summary financial statement contains the statements the subsection requires` `the summary financial statement states that it is only a summary of information in the company's annual financial statements or consolidated financial statements, and directors' statement` `the company has auditors` `the summary financial statement contains a statement by the company's auditors of their opinion on its consistency and compliance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of the company must ensure that the summary financial statements comply with the requirements referred to in subsections (5) and (6)" (a duty not met: the provision's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection (subsection (7) leaves subsection (6A) out of its offence): no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 203A(6A) (src:18971-18973)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 203A act`
`s 203A(6A) the directors must ensure that the summary financial statements comply` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 203A(6A) ensure that the summary financial statements comply with the requirements referred to in subsections (5) and (6)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not ensure that the summary financial statements comply with the requirements referred to in subsections (5) and (6)"

§ `Section 203A(7): the offence of default`

-- src:18977 | (7) If default is made in complying with this section other than
-- src:18978 | subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9), the
-- src:18979 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:18980 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:18981 | exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 203A(7) (src:18977-18981)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 203A other than subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203A(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 203A other than subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9)` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section other than subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md; "other than subsection (6A)" is one of the six left to the encoder: a default of (6A) alone is not an offence under this subsection)

@ref s 203A(7) (src:18977-18981)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 203A other than subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 203A(7) penalty`
`s 203A(7) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 203A(7) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 203A other than subsection (6A) or any regulations made under subsection (9)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 203A(7) penalty` OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "an offence" the subsection creates ("a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty"; the text gives no imprisonment, so the term is 0 months); where the person is not guilty of it the subsection fixes no penalty
